<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Book of Llandaff</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1125</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> · Also known as Liber Landavensis</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Book of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/llandaff">Llandaff</a> is a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manuscript">manuscript</a> compiled at Llandaff Cathedral in south-east <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wales">Wales</a> around 1125. Written to support the claims of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishops</a> of Llandaff, it contains saints' lives and about 150 charters recording land grants. Many charters preserve older material and name kings of early medieval Ergyng, Gwent and Glywysing who are otherwise little known.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/book-of-llandaff.jpg" alt="Book of Llandaff" width="320" height="454" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Liber_Lanavensis_f.5.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
